<title>DENMARK: Danish October reserves rise to 88.7 bln crowns.</title>
<headline>Danish October reserves rise to 88.7 bln crowns.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's foreign exchange reserves rose to 88.7 billion crowns at end-October 1996 from 83.9 billion crowns at end-September 1996, according to the central bank's monthly balance sheet released on Monday.  </p>
<p>DANISH RESERVES</p>
<p>				  Oct 1996   Sept 1996    Oct 1995</p>
<p>    Reserves (bln crowns)    88.7	 83.9	    64.4</p>
<p>NOTE - In a statement the Central Bank said net foreign loans in October were nil. The October foreign reserves compared with average analysts' expectations of 88.7 billion crowns, not taking into account state loan transactions.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33-969652</p>
</text>
